    "body": "The documented PEFT selectors for layers 0 and 1 also match layers 10–19 because `wildcard_match` treats a literal path separator (`.`) as a regex wildcard. This can silently attach adapters to extra layers, or exclude those layers unexpectedly.\n\nEscape periods before expanding `*`. A regression test exercises the existing `ModuleMatcher` target, exclusion and canonical-mapping paths over 24 layers. The production change is one line.\n\nEvidence: the [documented layer selectors](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/blob/2161fe922dc97e503eb1d52d644483066d8e99b0/docs/training/peft.md#L109) and [matcher helper](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/blob/2161fe922dc97e503eb1d52d644483066d8e99b0/src/megatron/bridge/peft/utils.py#L757). This follows the selector-contract investigation prompted by [Automodel #4045](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Automodel/pull/4045); no implementation was copied. Related [issue #1738](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/issues/1738) concerns unmatched targets, while this fixes overmatching. The candidate was carried forward from the [weekly landscape report](https://linear.app/nvidia/issue/MB-1745/weekly-landscape-learning-2026-10-03-pdt).\n\nValidation on base `2161fe922dc97e503eb1d52d644483066d8e99b0`, using the pinned MCore dependency and CPU tensors:\n\n- Fail before / pass after: `uv run python -m pytest tests/unit_tests/peft/test_module_matcher.py::TestModuleMatcher::test_layer_wildcards_preserve_path_separators -q` — 3 assertion failures before the production change; 3 passed afterward. The initial target/canonical selection included layers 10–19, and the exclusion path incorrectly omitted them.\n- Adjacent tests: `uv run python -m pytest tests/unit_tests/peft/test_module_matcher.py tests/unit_tests/peft/test_utils.py -k 'TestModuleMatcher or wildcard_match' -q` — 37 passed, 119 deselected.\n- `uv run pre-commit run --all-files` and `git diff --check` passed.\n- `uv run mypy --strict --no-incremental src/megatron/bridge/peft/utils.py tests/unit_tests/peft/test_module_matcher.py` reports 139 existing diagnostics on both the base and patched trees, with identical diagnostics after accounting for line offsets.\n- Separate read-only checklist review completed after the reviewer service could not start. Duplicate, ownership, minimal scope, red/green and publication checks passed.\n\nCurrent `main` was rechecked at `aea5c536903456835dabdeee7cb0925ba8208bdc`; the intervening PP-local export change does not touch the PEFT source, tests or documentation. No matching issue/PR implementation was found.\n\nNon-goals: expanding the matcher dialect, changing adapter/model scope, adding dependencies, modifying CI or public conversion signatures, or validating distributed training. This Draft fixes the documented layer-selection contract only.\n",
